<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairie harvest 30 pct complete - CWB.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairie harvest 30 pct complete - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairie harvest was about 30 percent completed by Monday, a Canadian Wheat Board weather and crop analyst told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It sounds like things got slowed down across the Prairies on the wetter weather last week. A week ago we thought we were about 20 percent harvested, so I'd say this week 30 percent is a reasonable preliminary estimate,&quot; CWB director of weather and crop surveillance Paul Bullock said.</p>
<p>There were slight frosts in the northern half of Alberta and northwestern Saskatchewan's grainbelt since September 4 when lows of 0.0 to -3.0 Celsius for one to two hours each night.</p>
<p>&quot;My own feeling is the frost's there but it's not a real big significant problem,&quot; Bullock said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
